// Curve25519 and Ed25519 in pure Mettle: the arithmetic behind X25519
// (RFC 7748) and Ed25519 (RFC 8032 section 5.1). Internal: used by kx.mettle
// and sign.mettle.
//
// Ported from Monocypher 4.0.3 (src/monocypher.c, curve and scalar code),
// Copyright (c) Loup Vaillant and contributors, BSD-2-Clause / CC0; see
// NOTICE. The field code is the ref10 design Monocypher uses: a field element
// is ten limbs of 25.5 bits (int32[10], radix 2^25.5) with int64 products and
// signed carries; points are in extended coordinates (a group element is
// int32[40]: X, Y, Z, T); the X25519 ladder is the Montgomery ladder; the
// fixed base multiplication is Monocypher's twin signed 4-bit combs over two
// precomputed tables; verification uses sliding windows (width 3 for the
// public key, width 5 over a precomputed table for the base point); scalars
// mod L use Monocypher's 32-bit word arithmetic and Barrett reduction.
//
// Not ported: Monocypher hashes EdDSA with BLAKE2b. This is Ed25519 as RFC
// 8032 says, with SHA-512, so the hashing and the message flow of sign and
// verify are cryptex's own; only the group and scalar arithmetic is
// Monocypher's.
//
// Constant time: everything that touches a scalar or a key (the X25519
// ladder, the base multiplication, the scalar arithmetic in signing, key
// generation) is a fixed sequence of operations with masked swaps and table
// reads; no branch, loop bound or index depends on secret data. Signature
// verification works on public data only and is variable time (the sliding
// windows, the point decoding and the small-order tests).

import "crypto/core/status";
import "crypto/core/util";
import "crypto/hash/sha2";

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Constants
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

